## Summary

Provide a concise overview of what changed and why it is needed.

Closes #(issue)

## Type of Change

- [ ] `feat`: New feature
- [ ] `fix`: Bug fix
- [ ] `refactor`: Code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
- [ ] `perf`: Performance improvement
- [ ] `docs`: Documentation only
- [ ] `test`: Adding or updating tests
- [ ] `chore`: Maintenance, tooling, or dependencies
- [ ] `ci`: CI/CD workflow changes

## How Has This Been Tested?

List the verification commands you ran and their results:

- [ ] Pre-commit hooks (`pre-commit run --all-files`)
- [ ] Automated test suite
- [ ] Manual verification (describe steps below if applicable)

## Checklist

- [ ] Branch was created from `main` and targets `main`.
- [ ] Pre-commit checks, linters, and tests pass without bypassing hooks.
- [ ] New and modified code includes clear docstrings and comments where needed.
- [ ] Documentation has been updated to match behavior changes.
- [ ] Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).
- [ ] No secrets or `.log/` files are included in the diff.
